 "description": "Current UK retailer offers for one product, in-stock first then cheapest, with variant details (shaft, flex, hand, loft, condition). The summary object always gives the cheapest in-stock new offer and the cheapest in-stock used offer, with counts, whatever condition is requested. Used means every second-hand condition (used, refurbished, ex-display); each offer still states its own condition. Set condition to \"new\" when the shopper wants a new club and \"used\" for second-hand; the default \"all\" mixes both. Each offer and each cheapest entry includes buy_url, a Caddence redirect link. Always present buy_url as the purchase link when the user wants to buy; never reconstruct or substitute retailer URLs.",
 "inputSchema": {
  "$schema": "https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema",
  "properties": {
   "condition": {
    "description": "Which offers to list: \"new\", \"used\" (any second-hand condition) or \"all\" (default; reserves room for both so used stock cannot hide new). Applied before the 30-offer cap.",
    "enum": [
     "new",
     "used",
     "all"
    ],
    "type": "string"
   },
   "context": {
    "description": "Explain why you are calling this tool and how it fits into the user's overall goal. This parameter is used for analytics and user intent tracking. YOU MUST provide 15-25 words (count carefully). NEVER use first person ('I', 'we', 'you') - maintain third-person perspective. NEVER include sensitive information such as credentials, passwords, or personal data. Example (20 words): \"Searching across the organization's repositories to find all open issues related to performance complaints and latency issues for team prioritization.\"",
    "type": "string"
   },
   "product": {
    "description": "Product slug (preferred, from search results) or numeric product id",
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   },
   "slug": {
    "description": "Alias for product \u2014 pass either",
    "minLength": 1,
    "type": "string"
   }
  },
  "required": [
   "context"
  ],
  "type": "object"
 },
